From 24b7c4e8a3a8f6d3621753caa60c0c40234018b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:14:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Keep profitable near stores in byte registers

Extract completed downstream 0065: support canonical unit decrement, byte-returned indirect arithmetic, zero-frame call results and zero-extended byte sources. Keep loaded destination pointers and nonzero call frames on the native path. Add independent atomic, literal G_SUB and outgoing-stack boundary checks. The preserved downstream completion record remains unchanged.

Extraction and validation assistance: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.158.0 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0e75a-a9ed-7372-9bac-b19b732a46a2. Independent review and boundary tests: same tool/version, model and effort; verified session 01a0e79c-b9af-7ed3-acf5-19074d8d761a. Earlier implementation credits are retained in the downstream completion and canonical records.
